   "ANSWER": "<ul data-end=\"612\" data-start=\"329\">\n\t<li data-end=\"511\" data-start=\"329\">\n\t<p data-end=\"511\" data-start=\"331\">Definition of Turnaround Time (in own words):<br data-end=\"379\" data-start=\"376\" />\n\t<em data-end=\"485\" data-start=\"381\">&quot;It is the total time taken to execute a process from the time it is submitted until it is completed.&nbsp;</em><span data-end=\"511\" data-start=\"492\">&nbsp;</span><strong data-end=\"511\" data-start=\"492\"> 50%</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"612\" data-start=\"513\">\n\t<p data-end=\"612\" data-start=\"515\">Correct formula:<br data-end=\"534\" data-start=\"531\" />\n\t<em data-end=\"586\" data-start=\"536\">Turnaround Time = Completion Time &ndash; Arrival Time&nbsp;&nbsp;</em><strong data-end=\"612\" data-start=\"593\">&nbsp;50%</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC202J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO4",
    "PLO12",
    "PLO13"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Define &quot;Turnaround Time&quot; and mention its formula.</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 301,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 12308
  },
  {
   "_id": 12311,
   "ANSWER": "<ul data-end=\"612\" data-start=\"329\">\n\t<li data-end=\"921\" data-start=\"751\">\n\t<p data-end=\"921\" data-start=\"753\"><strong data-end=\"799\" data-start=\"774\">&nbsp;Preemptive Scheduling</strong>:<br data-end=\"803\" data-start=\"800\" />\n\t<em data-end=\"895\" data-start=\"805\">The CPU can be taken away from a running process if a higher priority process arrives.&nbsp;</em><strong data-end=\"921\" data-start=\"902\">30%</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1093\" data-start=\"923\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1093\" data-start=\"925\"><span data-end=\"975\" data-start=\"946\">&nbsp;</span><strong data-end=\"975\" data-start=\"946\">Non-preemptive Scheduling</strong>:<br data-end=\"979\" data-start=\"976\" />\n\t<em data-end=\"1067\" data-start=\"981\">Once a process is allocated the CPU, it runs till termination or moves to waiting.&nbsp;</em><strong data-end=\"1093\" data-start=\"1074\">30%</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1221\" data-start=\"1095\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1221\" data-start=\"1097\">One valid example each for <strong data-end=\"1138\" data-start=\"1124\">preemptive</strong> and <strong data-end=\"1161\" data-start=\"1143\">non-preemptive</strong> (e.g., <em data-end=\"1182\" data-start=\"1169\">Round Robin</em> vs. <em data-end=\"1193\" data-start=\"1187\">FCFS</em>):&nbsp;<span data-end=\"1221\" data-start=\"1202\">&nbsp;</span><strong data-end=\"1221\" data-start=\"1202\">40%</strong></p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
