  {
   "_id": 18014,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"2722\" data-start=\"2445\">In operating systems, <strong data-end=\"2503\" data-start=\"2467\">Interprocess Communication (IPC)</strong> enables processes to exchange information and coordinate their execution. When multiple processes interact and share data, <strong data-end=\"2646\" data-start=\"2627\">synchronization</strong> becomes essential to maintain <strong data-end=\"2697\" data-start=\"2677\">data consistency</strong> and avoid <strong data-end=\"2721\" data-start=\"2708\">conflicts</strong>.</p>\n\n<hr data-end=\"2727\" data-start=\"2724\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"2774\" data-start=\"2729\"><strong data-end=\"2774\" data-start=\"2733\">Importance of Synchronization in IPC:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3053\" data-start=\"2776\">\n\t<li data-end=\"2874\" data-start=\"2776\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2874\" data-start=\"2778\"><strong data-end=\"2807\" data-start=\"2778\">Prevents race conditions:</strong> Ensures only one process accesses the shared resource at a time.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2963\" data-start=\"2875\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2963\" data-start=\"2877\"><strong data-end=\"2906\" data-start=\"2877\">Maintains data integrity:</strong> Synchronization avoids corrupted or inconsistent data.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3053\" data-start=\"2964\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3053\" data-start=\"2966\"><strong data-end=\"2996\" data-start=\"2966\">Ensures proper sequencing:</strong> Helps in coordinating execution order between processes.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"3058\" data-start=\"3055\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"3109\" data-start=\"3060\"><strong data-end=\"3109\" data-start=\"3064\">Common Synchronization Mechanisms in IPC:</strong></h3>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3136\" data-start=\"3111\"><strong data-end=\"3134\" data-start=\"3116\">1. Semaphores:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3137\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3192\" data-start=\"3137\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3192\" data-start=\"3139\">Integer variables used to signal between processes.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3193\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3207\" data-start=\"3195\">Two types:</p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3210\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3210\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3278\" data-start=\"3212\"><strong data-end=\"3241\" data-start=\"3212\">Binary Semaphore (Mutex):</strong> 0 or 1, used for mutual exclusion.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3281\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3358\" data-start=\"3283\"><strong data-end=\"3306\" data-start=\"3283\">Counting Semaphore:</strong> Allows limited access (e.g., for multiple readers).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3399\" data-start=\"3360\"><strong data-end=\"3397\" data-start=\"3365\">2. Mutex (Mutual Exclusion):</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3495\" data-start=\"3400\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3495\" data-start=\"3400\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3495\" data-start=\"3402\">A lock mechanism that ensures only <strong data-end=\"3452\" data-start=\"3437\">one process</strong> enters the <strong data-end=\"3484\" data-start=\"3464\">critical section</strong> at a time.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3520\" data-start=\"3497\"><strong data-end=\"3518\" data-start=\"3502\">3. Monitors:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3641\" data-start=\"3521\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3641\" data-start=\"3521\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3641\" data-start=\"3523\">A high-level synchronization construct that encapsulates shared data, procedures, and synchronization between threads.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3677\" data-start=\"3643\"><strong data-end=\"3675\" data-start=\"3648\">4. Condition Variables:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3784\" data-start=\"3678\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3784\" data-start=\"3678\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3784\" data-start=\"3680\">Used with monitors to allow a process to <strong data-end=\"3755\" data-start=\"3721\">wait until a condition is true</strong>, and then <strong data-end=\"3776\" data-start=\"3766\">signal</strong> others.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h4 data-end=\"3816\" data-start=\"3786\"><strong data-end=\"3814\" data-start=\"3791\">5. Message Passing:</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3817\">\n\t<li data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3817\">\n\t<p data-end=\"3894\" data-start=\"3819\">Processes communicate via <strong data-end=\"3853\" data-start=\"3845\">send</strong> and <strong data-end=\"3869\" data-start=\"3858\">receive</strong> operations. It can be:</p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3897\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3941\" data-start=\"3897\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3941\" data-start=\"3899\"><strong data-end=\"3915\" data-start=\"3899\">Synchronous:</strong> Blocking communication.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3944\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"3991\" data-start=\"3946\"><strong data-end=\"3963\" data-start=\"3946\">Asynchronous:</strong> Non-blocking communication.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"3996\" data-start=\"3993\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"4037\" data-start=\"3998\"><strong data-end=\"4037\" data-start=\"4002\">Issues Without Synchronization:</strong></h3>\n\n<ul data-end=\"4289\" data-start=\"4039\">\n\t<li data-end=\"4122\" data-start=\"4039\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4122\" data-start=\"4041\"><strong data-end=\"4061\" data-start=\"4041\">Race Conditions:</strong> Multiple processes updating shared variables simultaneously.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4123\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4197\" data-start=\"4125\"><strong data-end=\"4139\" data-start=\"4125\">Deadlocks:</strong> Two or more processes waiting on each other indefinitely.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"4289\" data-start=\"4198\">\n\t<p data-end=\"4289\" data-start=\"4200\"><strong data-end=\"4215\" data-start=\"4200\">Starvation:</strong> A process waits too long due to others repeatedly accessing the resource.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
